  <UADataType NodeId="i=65031" BrowseName="DataChannelDeliveryMode">
    <DisplayName>DataChannelDeliveryMode</DisplayName>
    <Description>The delivery guarantee requested for a data channel. What a mode can actually deliver depends on the transport: only a transport with a lossy path can genuinely drop data in flight, so over opc.tcp and opc.wss the lossy modes degrade to sender-side discard.</Description>
    <Category>Data Channels Data Types</Category>
    <References>
      <Reference ReferenceType="HasSubtype" IsForward="false">i=29</Reference>
      <Reference ReferenceType="HasProperty">i=65931</Reference>
    </References>
    <Definition Name="DataChannelDeliveryMode"><Field Name="ReliableOrdered" Value="0"><Description>Every frame is delivered, in order. The default, and the only mode a purely reliable transport realizes exactly.</Description></Field><Field Name="ReliableUnordered" Value="1"><Description>Every frame is delivered, but the receiver may hand frames to the application as they arrive rather than buffering to restore order.</Description></Field><Field Name="PartiallyReliable" Value="2"><Description>A frame is retried until its deadline passes or MaxRetransmits is reached, then abandoned and reported in a gap notification.</Description></Field><Field Name="Unreliable" Value="3"><Description>A frame is sent once and never retried. Frames still queued when their deadline passes are discarded.</Description></Field></Definition>
  </UADataType>
