    <Definition Name="DataChannelState"><Field Name="Opening" Value="0"><Description>OpenDataChannel has been accepted and the endpoint is being prepared; no frame may be sent for this ChannelId until the response has been handed to the transport.</Description></Field><Field Name="Open" Value="1"><Description>Payload may flow in the negotiated directions.</Description></Field><Field Name="Paused" Value="2"><Description>The channel is open but the peer's flow control credit is exhausted in this direction, so no payload may be sent. Over opc.quic this is QUIC stream or connection blocking instead.</Description></Field><Field Name="Closing" Value="3"><Description>An orderly half-close is in progress; already queued frames are still being drained and no new payload may be enqueued.</Description></Field><Field Name="Closed" Value="4"><Description>The channel is closed. Its ChannelId is not reassigned while the owning SecureChannel remains open.</Description></Field><Field Name="Faulted" Value="5"><Description>The channel was aborted by a RESET frame, by a timeout, or by loss of the SecureChannel, Session or authorizing user identity.</Description></Field></Definition>
